<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12659" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποθύμιος</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῡ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span> (fem. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ίη</span> in <i><span class="en">
			Semon.
			7.35
		</span></i>): (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θῡμός</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>not according to the mind,
				unpleasant, hateful,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔπος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					710
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποθύμια ἔρδειν τινί</span> to
			do one <i>a disfavour,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				14.261
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὔ τι ἀποθύμιον ποιῆσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					7.168
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή μοί τι τέκνοις ἀ. ἕρπῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Mosch.
					4.93
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
